    "narrative": "Today\u2019s optimal lineup for the Austin Waves is anchored by three high-upside plays against favorable matchups. **Kyle Tucker** leads the board with a 76.70 efficiency score, benefiting significantly from a soft matchup against JP Sears (5.11 xERA) and an expected move into the middle of the order. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) and **Andy Pages** (71.11) follow closely, both capitalizing on elevated SP skill metrics and positive park factors. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** specifically draws value from a strong platoon advantage against Chandler, while **Andy Pages** remains a high-floor play despite a slight penalty for facing a pitcher with a high stolen base hold rate. **Gunnar Henderson** rounds out the top tier at 70.61; while he faces a tougher arm in Lodolo, his elite base projection keeps him in the must-start category.\n\nThe most difficult decision was the final bench spot, where **Nolan Schanuel** (49.79) narrowly missed the cut over **Miguel Vargas** (54.55). While **Nolan Schanuel** offers reliability, **Miguel Vargas** was prioritized due to his elite xwOBA (0.406) and the organizational mandate to maximize output in the 5x5 categories. We continue to monitor the status of **Liam Hicks**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Kyle Tucker**, **Andy Pages**, and **Heliot Ramos**, all of whom carry \"Lineup Pending\" tags. While we have projected their spots based on historical data, late-afternoon shifts\u2014particularly for **Jackson Merrill**\u2014could necessitate a pivot if those slots fall lower in the order. \n\nWe are also paying close attention to the base-stealing environments for **Andy Pages** and **Heliot Ramos**. While **Heliot Ramos** (61.74) is bolstered by a favorable park and a slow delivery from Gordon, the risk associated with facing elite hold pitchers remains a secondary factor in our final assessment. All players currently in the starting nine are clear of significant weather warnings, but the margin between **Coby Mayo** (66.72) and our bench depth remains razor-thin; should any of the pending lineups confirm lower-than-projected batting spots, we will be prepared to swap in **Nolan Schanuel** or **Denzer Guzman** to ensure we aren't wasting daily game caps on sub-optimal efficiency.",
